% Selected bibliography for the proposed introduction.
% Checked on 2026-09-09. This file makes no claim to identify the earliest
% complete proof of the all-n absolute-cosine minimum theorem.
% Gusyatnikov1980: an original Kvant problem-solution article; its final
% exercises include the n=4 bound. Do not describe every appended exercise
% as a theorem proved in that article. The printed signature is P. Gusyatnikov
% (Cyrillic: П. Гусятников); the given name is deliberately not expanded.
% HDD2022: a public mathematical problem with proposed reductions, not a
% journal paper or a verified complete proof. Consult its revision history.
% AlzerLiuShi2013 and AlzerVolkmer2026: publisher abstracts and bibliographies
% were inspected; their complete texts were not obtained during this search.
% AlzerKwong2017 treats squared sine/cosine terms, not termwise absolute values.

